export const AGREEMENT_TEXT = "Aircraft Rental Agreement\n\nThis agreement is between Fire Hound Rental, hereinafter referred to as the \u201cOperator,\u201d and the \u201cRenter\u201d identified in the signature section of this agreement regarding the use of the designated aircraft hereinafter referred to as the \u201caircraft.\u201d\n\nA.\n(1) Renter acknowledges and agrees that the aircraft is the property of the Operator.\n(2) Renter acknowledges that he has inspected the aircraft and has found it to be in good mechanical condition and airworthy. Renter has inspected the aircraft for any damage and noted such damage on the renter invoice.\n(3) Renter agrees to return the aircraft at the scheduled time, weather permitting.\n(4) Renter agrees to properly secure the aircraft in its hangar after each flight.\n\nB.\nRenter expressly acknowledges personal liability to pay Operator on demand or immediately at the completion of the rental period:\n(1) Service and time charges computed at the applicable posted rates until said aircraft is returned to its hangar and rental period is completed. Acceptable forms of payment are cash or check only.\n(2) Any loss or damage to the aircraft, its components, parts or equipment during the rental period will be paid for by the renter or the renter\u2019s insurance. If the damage results in the aircraft being removed from service, the renter agrees to pay the operator for two hours per day at the current hourly rental rates until said aircraft is returned to airworthy condition.\n(3) The hangar is under 24 hour video surveillance. Any damage to the aircraft that is not reported will cause the renter to lose flight privileges.\n\nC.\nRenter agrees not to tamper with, molest, or attempt to repair any parts of the aircraft or its accessories, but will contact the Operator for instructions upon encountering mechanical malfunctions or any damage to the aircraft.\n\nD.\nRenter agrees to report any aircraft damage, accident or incident to the Operator at the completion of rental period or as soon as possible.\n\nE.\nRenter agrees that rented aircraft shall not be used or operated:\n(1) For any illegal purposes.\n(2) In any race, speed test, or contest.\n(3) By any person other than the Renter who signed the agreement.\n(4) Outside the limits of the Continental United States.\n(5) To carry passengers or property for compensation or hire.\n(6) For any flight for which the Renter is not properly rated or certified.\n\nF.\nRenter agrees to sign and comply with future renter guides provided by Fire Hound Rental.\n\nG. Cancellation Policy.\nReservations cancelled less than twenty-four (24) hours prior to the scheduled rental start time are subject to a $50 cancellation fee. Reservations cancelled twenty-four (24) hours or more prior to the scheduled rental start time are not subject to a cancellation fee. Cancellations due to weather are exempt from this fee.\n\nH.\nRenter, by affixing his signature hereon, does agree to follow the following flight operations safety rules, emergency maintenance procedures and insurance provisions.\n\nFLIGHT OPERATIONS SAFETY RULES\n\u2022 Pilot Certificate \u2013 Renter must hold a valid and current pilot certificate and/or student pilot certificate with appropriate ratings. The Renter will fly the aircraft from the left seat, and he/she will be responsible for the aircraft and its operation at all times.\n\u2022 Currency \u2013 Renter must possess evidence of a current biennial flight review, medical certificate, and aircraft checkout by a pilot designated by the Operator.\n\u2022 Preflight \u2013 Renter will personally conduct a preflight inspection of the aircraft as prescribed by the manufacturer. Renter shall use the manufacturer\u2019s recommended pre-takeoff, cruise and pre-landing checklists.\n\u2022 Weather \u2013 Renter shall plan to operate the aircraft only when the present and forecasted weather indicates VFR conditions local and in route (ceiling of at least 3,000 feet and visibility 5 miles or greater) unless otherwise approved by CFI or Renter is instrument rated, current for IFR.\n\u2022 Take-off and landing area \u2013 No take-off or landing shall be made on any area other than the runways of an airport designed, constructed, maintained, and used as an airport with runways of no less than 2,000 feet. Runway lengths shorter than 2,000 feet must be approved by CFI.\n\u2022 Physical conditions \u2013 Renter shall not operate the aircraft for a period of at least 12 hours after using any intoxicating substances such as liquor, tranquilizers, and sleeping aids.\n\u2022 The Renter will comply with all local, state and federal regulations.\n\nTRANSIENT MAINTENANCE POLICY\n\u2022 In the event of a breakdown, notify the Operator of the problem immediately. If maintenance personnel are not available leave your name, aircraft number and telephone number where you can be contacted.\n\u2022 Do not authorize any repairs to be made to the aircraft without clearance from the Operator representative. Failure to do so could result in the Renter being responsible for a portion or the entirety of the bill.\n\u2022 The Operator will reimburse the Renter for fuel purchased, provided that the Renter presents a fuel receipt from the place of purchase that shows the number of gallons, and price purchased.\n\u2022 All repairs and fueling will be made by properly licensed facilities and personnel.\n\nNOTICE OF INSURANCE COVERAGE\nRenters are required to purchase an \u201cAircraft Renters Insurance Policy\u201d of a minimum value of $60,000.00 from an independent insurance company to protect themselves in situations where they may be found to be negligent or responsible for damages. In the event the repairs exceed the renter\u2019s insurance policy value or the aircraft replacement, the renter agrees to cover any costs not covered by the renter\u2019s insurance policy. The safety of any passengers or persons present in the vicinity of the aircraft or in the hangar other than renter will be the responsibility of the renter. Fire Hound Rental reserves the right to increase the value of Renters Insurance required at will.\n\nI HAVE READ AND I UNDERSTAND THE ABOVE COVENANTS, RESTRICTIONS AND REQUIREMENTS OF THE RENTAL AGREEMENT. I ACKNOWLEDGE THAT I HAVE RECEIVED A COPY OF THIS AGREEMENT.\n\nName: _______________________________    Renter\nSignature: ___________________________    Date: ______________    Renter\n\n*If renter is a minor a parent or legal guardian must also sign.\n\nName: _______________________________    Parent / Legal Guardian\nSignature: ___________________________    Date: ______________    Parent / Legal Guardian\n";
